# Binary files — prevent Git from applying autocrlf line-ending
# normalisation on Windows checkouts. The Phase-1 commit of the land
# mask shipped 810001 bytes instead of 810000 because this file was
# missing; bytes 0x0a were silently rewritten to 0x0d0a on check-in.
*.bin binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Machine-generated catalogues are written with LF by their generator
# (scripts/generate-airline-catalog.ts) and byte-compared against fresh
# generator output by the drift-guard test
# (backend/src/__tests__/dataIntegrity.airlineCatalog.test.ts). With
# core.autocrlf=true these files check out as CRLF on Windows, so the
# byte compare (LF generator vs CRLF on disk) failed. Pin LF so the guard
# is platform-stable.
frontend/src/lib/generated/*.ts text eol=lf
